New character...going down to level 2.
"You hear someone cursing shoplifters."
oh, good!  A shop to rob!
(explore level for a while)
open a door, and... WHOPPING HUGE SHOP!!!!!!!!  This was probably the 
biggest shop I've ever seen.  The room was 6 x 11, with 59 objects and
one obvious mimic.  (Reversed armor symbol)

It was an armor dealership (could be worse) so I thought I'd just rob it
and boost my armor class.  (Found a ring of teleport on level 1.)  My pet was 
dead so I couldn't check for cursed stuff.  Oh, well.  I stripped out of my
leather armor and started putting stuff on...
Wear Hawaiian shirt.	AC: 10 (+0, oh well.)
Wear bronze plate	AC:  4 (ditto)
Wear faded pall		AC:  2 (+1 elven cloak...nice.)
Wear hiking boots	AC:  6 (-5 _fumble_ boots ?!?  *choke*!)
Wear padded gloves	AC:  7 (-2 Gauntlets of Fumbling.  UGH!)
Wear visored helm	AC: 10 (-4 cursed Helm of Brilliance.  HURL!!!)
By this time, I was mightily peeved, and then I picked up the next object.
"You get a blast of power from the long sword named Fire Brand. --more--"
"You die."
GRRRRR!!!!
When checking my inventory, I noticed that out of five pairs of boots, three
sets of gloves, and three helmets in that shop, not one of them was helpful!
They were _all_ cursed (-n) normal or harmful objects.  There wasn't a single
shield or non-elven cloak in the place, either...  What a lousy shop!  If I'd
been playing a neutral priest instead of a rogue it would have been a different
story...

